IMPORT prelude

-- Registered Designs Act 2000 (Singapore) -- what counts as a design (s 2(1)), who owns it (s 4), what may be registered (ss 5, 6, 7,
-- 8A), Convention priority (s 12(1)(c)), how long registration lasts (s 21), what infringes and what does not (ss 30, 31, 36(3)),
-- the innocent infringer (s 39), late ownership challenges (s 23(4)), groundless threats (s 44), and the offences (ss 65, 66, 68).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RDA2000.txt. The deposit
-- labels itself "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 9/3/2025"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 5 of 2025 (wef
-- 9 March 2025), in Part 6A, which this row does not encode. The sections encoded carry annotations to Act 7 of 2022, Act 31 of
-- 2022, Act 25 of 2021 and Act 23 of 2019.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 8 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a designer, a business
-- selling products, or a practitioner advising either actually meets. Not encoded: the application procedure and examination
-- (ss 11, 13-20), the pre-30 October 2017 disclosure rules (s 8) and the s 8B transitional window, artistic works (ss 9, 22),
-- subsequent registrations (s 10), revocation procedure (s 27), co-ownership and transactions (ss 33-35), delivery up and disposal
-- (ss 40, 41), Government use (Part 4), the Registrar (Part 5), the Hague Agreement (Part 5A), border measures (Part 6A), and every
-- "prescribed" period, fee and form (left to rules not retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Registered Designs Act 2000 -- designs`

§§ `2(1) -- what a design is`

-- s 2(1): "design" means "features of shape, configuration, colours, pattern or ornament applied to any article or non-physical
-- product that give that article or non-physical product its appearance", but does not include (a) "a method or principle of
-- construction"; (b) features of shape, configuration or colours that (i) "are dictated solely by the function" the thing has to
-- perform, (ii) "are dependent upon the appearance of another article" of which it is intended to form an integral part, or (iii)
-- enable it to be connected to, or placed in, around or against, another so that either may perform its function; or (c) "features
-- consisting only of one or more colours" not used with any feature of shape or configuration and not giving rise to pattern or
-- ornament.
DECLARE Feature IS ONE OF
    `a distinctive shape`
    `a surface pattern`
    `ornament`
    `colours used with a shape`
    `a method of construction`
    `a shape dictated solely by function`
    `a shape that must match the larger product`
    `a shape that lets it connect to another product`
    `colour alone with no shape or pattern`

GIVEN `the feature` IS A Feature
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the feature counts as design` IF
    CONSIDER `the feature`
    WHEN `a method of construction` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a shape dictated solely by function` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a shape that must match the larger product` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a shape that lets it connect to another product` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `colour alone with no shape or pattern` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4 -- who owns a design`

-- s 4(1): "the designer of a design is to be treated ... as the owner". (2) a design "created by an employee in the course of his or
-- her employment" -- the employer; (3) "subject to any agreement to the contrary". (5) a design "generated by computer in
-- circumstances such that there is no human designer" -- "the person by whom the arrangements necessary for the creation of the
-- design are made is deemed to be the designer". Assignment and transmission (s 4(4)) are not encoded.
DECLARE Owner IS ONE OF
    `the designer`
    `the employer`
    `the person who made the arrangements`

GIVEN `computer-generated with no human designer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `created by an employee in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `agreement to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Owner
`the first owner` MEANS
    IF `computer-generated with no human designer`
    THEN `the person who made the arrangements`
    ELSE IF `created by an employee in the course of employment` AND (NOT `agreement to the contrary`)
         THEN `the employer`
         ELSE `the designer`

§§ `8A -- disclosures that do not destroy novelty`

-- s 8A(1): an application must not be refused, nor a registration revoked, "by reason only of" (a) a disclosure to a person other
-- than the designer or successor "under conditions of confidentiality (whether express or implied)"; (b) a disclosure by the designer
-- or successor "during the period of 12 months immediately before the date of filing"; (c) a disclosure by another person in that
-- 12 months "in consequence of information provided, or any other action taken, by the designer"; (d) a disclosure in that 12 months
-- "as a consequence of an abuse in relation to the designer". (2): only disclosures "made on or after 30 October 2017".
--
-- Note (a) carries no time limit. A disclosure by a stranger acting independently is not on the list at all.
-- "Within 12 months" is read here as at most 12 whole months before filing (inference: the text counts a period, not whole months).
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `confidential disclosure`
    `disclosure by the designer`
    `disclosure by another using the designer's information`
    `disclosure resulting from an abuse of the designer`
    `independent disclosure by a stranger`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure, `months before filing` IS A NUMBER, `made on or after 30 October 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is disregarded` IF
        `made on or after 30 October 2017`
    AND CONSIDER `the disclosure`
        WHEN `confidential disclosure` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `independent disclosure by a stranger` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `months before filing` AT MOST 12

§§ `5, 6, 7 -- registrable designs`

-- s 5(1): "a design which is new may ... be registered". (2) not new if "the same as a design" (a) registered on a prior application,
-- or (b) "published in Singapore or elsewhere" before the application, "or if it differs from such a design only in immaterial details
-- or in features which are variants commonly used in the trade".
-- s 6: not registrable "if the publication or use of it would be contrary to public order or morality".
-- s 7(1): "No computer program or layout-design may be registered".
GIVEN `same as or immaterially different from an earlier design` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the only earlier publication is disregarded under s 8A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the design is new` IF
    (NOT `same as or immaterially different from an earlier design`) OR `the only earlier publication is disregarded under s 8A`

GIVEN `is new` IS A BOOLEAN, `contrary to public order or morality` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a computer program or layout-design` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the design is registrable` IF
    `is new` AND (NOT `contrary to public order or morality`) AND (NOT `is a computer program or layout-design`)

§§ `12(1)(c) -- Convention priority`

-- s 12(1)(c): "within 6 months after the date on which the first Convention application is filed", the applicant or successor applies
-- here; (2) the application is then treated, for novelty, "as filed on the date on which the first Convention application was filed".
-- The documentary conditions in (1)(d) and the refiling rule in (7) are not encoded.
GIVEN `was the first Convention application` IS A BOOLEAN, `months after the Convention filing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `priority may be claimed` IF
    `was the first Convention application` AND `months after the Convention filing` AT MOST 6

§§ `21 -- duration`

-- s 21(1): "The initial period of registration of a design is 5 years from the date of registration". (2) it "may be extended for a
-- second and third period of 5 years". (4) if not extended before expiry, registration "ceases to be in force ... and must be removed
-- from the Register". (5) restoration on a late application within "the prescribed period" (not encoded: the period is prescribed).
GIVEN `extensions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the allowed extensions` MEANS
    IF `extensions` GREATER THAN 2
    THEN 2
    ELSE IF `extensions` LESS THAN 0
         THEN 0
         ELSE `extensions`

GIVEN `extensions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years of protection` MEANS 5 TIMES (1 PLUS `the allowed extensions` `extensions`)

GIVEN `years since registration` IS A NUMBER, `extensions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration is in force` IF
    `years since registration` LESS THAN `the years of protection` `extensions`

§§ `30, 31 -- infringement`

-- s 30(1): exclusive rights (a) "to make in Singapore, or import into Singapore, for sale or hire, or for use for the purpose of trade
-- or business" and (b) "to sell, hire, or offer or expose for sale or hire, in Singapore", articles bearing the design "or a design
-- not substantially different". (2) infringed by any person who "without the consent of the registered owner and while the
-- registration is in force" does any of those things.
-- (5) not infringed by "any act for a private non-commercial purpose" or "for the purpose of evaluation, analysis, research or
-- teaching". (6) not infringed by reproducing a feature excluded by para (b) or (c) of the definition of "design".
-- (7) not infringed by import or sale of an article "placed on the market, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, by or with the consent
-- (conditional or otherwise) of the registered owner".
-- s 31(1): a person who before the date of registration did "in good faith in Singapore" an infringing act, or made "in good faith
-- effective and serious preparations" to do it, "has the right to continue". (3) that right "does not include a right to grant a
-- licence".
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `making copies for sale`
    `importing copies for sale`
    `selling copies`
    `offering copies for hire`
    `making a copy for private non-commercial use`
    `making a copy for research or teaching`
    `importing genuine goods first sold abroad by the owner`
    `copying only the functional or must-fit features`

GIVEN `the act` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is within the exclusive rights` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `making copies for sale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `importing copies for sale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling copies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `offering copies for hire` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the act` IS A Dealing, `owner consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `registration in force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prior good-faith user before registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act infringes` IF
        `the act is within the exclusive rights` `the act`
    AND (NOT `owner consented`)
    AND `registration in force`
    AND (NOT `prior good-faith user before registration`)

GIVEN `has the s 31 right` IS A BOOLEAN, `wants to license others` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prior user may do what it wants` IF
    `has the s 31 right` AND (NOT `wants to license others`)

§§ `36(3), 39 -- when proceedings and money remedies are available`

-- s 36(3): "no proceedings may be taken for an infringement of a registered design committed before the date on which the certificate
-- of registration of the design is issued under section 18".
-- s 39(1): the Court "must not award damages, nor make an order for an account of profits, against a defendant who proves that at the
-- date of the infringement the defendant was not aware, and had no reasonable grounds for believing, that the design in question was
-- registered". (2) the word "registered" on the article is not enough "unless the registration number of the design accompanied" it.
-- An injunction (s 36(2)(a)) is not barred by s 39.
GIVEN `infringed before the certificate issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings may be taken` IF
    NOT `infringed before the certificate issued`

DECLARE Marking IS ONE OF
    `no marking`
    `marked registered without the number`
    `marked registered with the number`

GIVEN `defendant actually knew` IS A BOOLEAN, `the marking` IS A Marking, `other reasonable grounds to believe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages or profits may be awarded` IF
        `defendant actually knew`
    OR  `other reasonable grounds to believe`
    OR  CONSIDER `the marking`
        WHEN `marked registered with the number` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `23(4) -- late challenges to ownership`

-- s 23(4): an application made "after the end of the period of 2 years from the date of issue of the certificate of registration" --
-- no order transferring a right "on the ground that the registered owner was not entitled to be registered as the owner, unless it
-- is shown that the registered owner knew" at the time of registration or transfer that it was not entitled.
-- "After the end of 2 years" is read as strictly more than 2 years (inference).
GIVEN `years after the certificate` IS A NUMBER, `registered owner knew it was not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a transfer order for non-entitlement is possible` IF
    (`years after the certificate` AT MOST 2) OR `registered owner knew it was not entitled`

§§ `44 -- groundless threats`

-- s 44(1): where a person "threatens any other person with proceedings for infringement", "any person aggrieved" may sue. (2) the
-- claimant "is entitled to such relief unless" (d) "the defendant proves" the acts "constitute, or if done would constitute, an
-- infringement" and (e) "the claimant fails to show that the registration ... is invalid". (3) no action "as regards a threat to bring
-- proceedings for an infringement alleged to consist of the making or importing of anything". (4) "a notification that a design is
-- registered does not of itself constitute a threat". (5) an advocate and solicitor acting for a client is not liable.
DECLARE Threat IS ONE OF
    `threat about selling`
    `threat about making or importing`
    `bare notice that the design is registered`

GIVEN `the threat` IS A Threat, `made by a solicitor for a client` IS A BOOLEAN, `defendant proves infringement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `claimant shows registration invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `threats relief is available` IF
        (NOT `made by a solicitor for a client`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the threat`
         WHEN `threat about selling` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND ((NOT `defendant proves infringement`) OR `claimant shows registration invalid`)

§§ `65, 66, 68 -- offences`

-- s 65: falsifying the Register -- "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or to both".
-- s 66(1): falsely representing that a design on goods "disposed of by the person for value" is registered -- "$10,000" or "12 months";
-- (3) the same penalty for marking goods, "after the right in a registered design has expired", with anything implying a subsisting
-- right.
-- s 68(1): a compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum
-- fine" and (b) "$5,000". Which offences are compoundable is prescribed by regulations (not retrieved).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `falsifying the Register`
    `falsely claiming registration`
    `marking goods after the right expired`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `falsifying the Register` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `falsifying the Register` THEN 60
    OTHERWISE 12

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

GIVEN `sold for value` IS A BOOLEAN, `marked as registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `actually registered for that product` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false-registration offence is committed` IF
    `sold for value` AND `marked as registered` AND (NOT `actually registered for that product`)
